<title>JAPAN: Enix to develop software for PlayStation.</title>
<headline>Enix to develop software for PlayStation.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese videogame software maker Enix Corp said on Thursday it had agreed with Sony Computer Entertainment to develop and sell software for the PlayStation 32-bit game players.</p>
<p>Enix will continue development and sales of software for Nintendo Co 's game players, Enix said in a statement.</p>
<p>The impact of the agreement with Sony Computer Entertainment on earnings is not yet known, Enix said.</p>
<p>Sony Computer Entertainment is a unit of Sony  6758 T Corp.</p>
